---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Me"
  description="How Kevin Castro approaches building secure, AI-powered systems in high-stakes, regulated domains."
>
  <main>
    <h1>// about</h1>
    <article class="text-content bracket-frame">
      <span class="corner tl"></span><span class="corner tr"></span>
      <span class="corner bl"></span><span class="corner br"></span>
      <p>
        I'm a senior software engineer who builds AI-powered and or
        data-intensive systems in high-stakes, regulated domains. My deepest
        experience is in healthcare (PHI-compliant infrastructure, HIPAA-grade
        data exchange, high-volume transaction processing), but the same
        discipline carries into energy and other regulated spaces: agentic
        document-reasoning pipelines, LLM and RAG infrastructure, and the eval
        frameworks that keep them honest in production. I own things end-to-end,
        from architecture through deployment.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work best dropped into a team as a paratrooper: I have full-stack
        range, I'm comfortable across frontend, backend, and infrastructure, and
        I'm able to make an immediate impact without a long ramp. I collaborate
        closely with product, domain experts, and leadership to shape both the
        architecture and the roadmap, not just execute against a spec handed to
        me.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm drawn to software where there's a short, traceable causal loop
        between the code and the human outcome: a healthcare API that gets a
        patient the right information, or an extraction pipeline that gets an
        analyst the right lease terms. I believe in craftsmanship in software,
        and I think that matters more, not less, as AI makes it easier to ship
        something that merely looks correct.
      </p>
      <p>
        I started in Mathematics and Physics at Claremont McKenna College before
        shifting into software full-time, training through UCSD Extension's
        Full-Stack Web Development bootcamp. I later earned a Bachelor of
        Science in Computer Science from Western Governors University in 2026,
        completed while working full-time.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  main {
    width: var(--reader-width);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 1.6em;
    margin-bottom: 0.75em;
  }
</style>
